# AI Study Companion - Base Rules

## Project Overview

- **Product**: Persistent AI learning companion for tutoring platform
- **Timeline**: 48-hour MVP sprint
- **Tech Stack**: React + Firebase + Cloud Run + Pinecone + OpenAI
- **Team**: Solo developer (Ankit)

## Key Constraints

- 48-hour deadline (firm)
- Mock student data only (5 students, 15 transcripts)
- All 6 core features in MVP: Auth, Chat, Quiz, Dashboard, Recommendations, Nudges
- Production-ready code (will be reused)
- Cost-conscious: Use GPT-4o-mini, Pinecone free tier, Firebase free tier where possible

## Code Philosophy

### 1. React Component Standards

- **Functional components + hooks only** (no class components)
- **Small, focused components** (<200 lines each)
- **Components folder**: Presentational components only
- **Pages folder**: Page-level routing components
- **Hooks pattern**: Extract logic into custom hooks (`useAuth`, `useFirestore`, `useAPI`)
- **Context API**: For shared state (AuthContext, ChatContext)
- **useReducer**: For complex state (chat messages - future extensibility: text → image → audio)

### 2. Styling

- **Tailwind CSS only** (no CSS files or styled-components)
- **Custom colors**: Indigo-600 (primary), Teal-500 (secondary) - defined in config
- **Responsive**: Mobile-first approach, test on desktop/tablet/mobile
- **No inline styles**: Use Tailwind classes only

### 3. Firebase Integration

- **Auth**: `onAuthStateChanged()` for session persistence
- **Firestore**: Use `onSnapshot()` listeners for real-time updates (no polling)
- **Cloud Storage**: Mock data uploads during MVP
- **Security**: Firestore rules enforce user isolation (no cross-student data access)
- **Token Management**: Firebase SDK auto-handles refresh

### 4. Backend Architecture

- **Cloud Functions**: Lightweight triggers (auth, recommendations, nudges)
- **Cloud Run**: Heavy AI workloads (chat, quiz generation, RAG retrieval)
- **LangChain**: For RAG orchestration + prompt templating
- **Pinecone**: Vector DB queries filtered by `student_id` (isolation)
- **OpenAI**: GPT-4o-mini for all LLM tasks (speed + cost)

### 5. API Design

- **All endpoints**: Firebase auth required (validate token in middleware)
- **Request format**: JSON with `student_id`, `conversation_id`, `message`
- **Response format**: Consistent `{ data, error, status }` structure
- **Error handling**: Return descriptive errors + user-friendly messages
- **Latency targets**: Chat <2s, Quiz <3s, Dashboard <1s

### 6. Data Model

- **Firestore collections**: users, students, goals, session_transcripts, conversations, quizzes, quiz_results, recommendations, nudge_logs, events
- **Document structure**: Flat where possible, subcollections for large datasets
- **Timestamps**: Always use `admin.firestore.Timestamp.now()` (server time)
- **IDs**: Use Firestore auto-generated IDs (not UUIDs)

### 7. Error Handling

- **Frontend**: `react-hot-toast` for all user-facing errors
- **Console logging**: Debug logs (development) vs error logs (production)
- **User messages**: Clear, actionable error text (no technical jargon)
- **API errors**: Return HTTP status + error code + message

### 8. Performance

- **Lazy load**: Firebase SDK only when needed
- **Batch queries**: Combine multiple Firestore reads where possible
- **Real-time optimization**: Only attach listeners to visible components
- **Image optimization**: Compress before upload to Storage
- **API caching**: Cache embedding results (don't re-embed same text)

### 9. Security

- **.env files**: Never commit (add to .gitignore)
- **Firebase rules**: Enforce strict user/student isolation
- **Token validation**: Cloud Run middleware validates all requests
- **Pinecone filters**: All queries include `student_id` filter
- **Secrets**: Use environment variables, never hardcode API keys

### 10. Git Workflow

- **Commits**: Every 4-6 hours with descriptive messages
- **Branches**: Main only (single developer)
- **Messages**: Clear, feature-focused (e.g., "Phase 3: Chat agent with RAG")

## File Structure (Strict Adherence)

```
/frontend/src
├── pages/          (Page-level components)
├── components/     (Reusable UI components)
├── contexts/       (React Context: AuthContext, ChatContext)
├── hooks/          (Custom hooks: useAuth, useFirestore, useAPI)
├── services/       (Business logic: api.js for all HTTP calls)
└── firebase.js     (Firebase initialization + config)

/functions/src
├── index.js        (Exports all functions)
├── auth.js         (Auth triggers)
├── recommendations.js  (Goal completion trigger)
├── scheduledNudges.js  (Hourly scheduled function)
└── services/       (Shared logic)

/cloud-run/src
├── index.js        (Express server setup)
├── middleware/     (Auth validation)
├── routes/         (Express routes)
└── services/       (Business logic: chat, quiz, embeddings)
```

## Testing Strategy

- **Manual end-to-end**: Test each feature before moving to next phase
- **Firebase Emulator**: Local development (Auth, Firestore, Functions)
- **DevTools**: Network/Performance monitoring for latency
- **Test Accounts**: 5 mock students with realistic data
- **Error Scenarios**: Network failures, expired tokens, LLM timeouts

## Deployment Checklist

- [ ] Environment variables configured
- [ ] Firestore rules deployed
- [ ] Cloud Storage rules deployed
- [ ] Cloud Functions deployed
- [ ] Cloud Run deployed
- [ ] All endpoints returning 200 OK
- [ ] Real-time listeners working
- [ ] README.md complete
- [ ] API.md complete
- [ ] ARCHITECTURE.md complete

## Common Pitfalls to Avoid

1. **Hardcoding API keys** → Use .env files
2. **Cross-user data leakage** → Always filter by student_id in Pinecone
3. **Forgetting auth token validation** → All Cloud Run endpoints require token
4. **Not chunking transcripts** → Large transcripts exceed OpenAI token limits
5. **Overusing Cloud Functions** → Use Cloud Run for compute-heavy tasks
6. **Firestore permission errors** → Deploy security rules early
7. **Real-time listener bloat** → Only attach to visible components
8. **LLM output parsing** → Use structured JSON format (response_format: { type: "json_object" })

